# --- Extension build-time config (Vite), NOT Chrome runtime ---
#
# Chrome extensions do not read a ".env" file in the browser. At runtime there is
# no Node-style process.env. Optional URL injection uses window.__JUSTWORK_BACKEND_URL__
# (e.g. tests) or this build-time value:
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to extension code via import.meta.env
# and are bundled into the shipped JS — treat them as public (never put secrets here).
#
# Copy lines you need into `.env` or `.env.local` at the repository root (gitignored),
# then run `yarn build`.

# Public default matches DEFAULT_BACKEND_URL unless you override:
# VITE_JUSTWORK_BACKEND_URL=https://api.tool.justwork.txzy.net
#
# Local development override:
# VITE_JUSTWORK_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1446
